<title>USA: Southwest Water Q4 shr rises to $0.20.</title>
<headline>Southwest Water Q4 shr rises to $0.20.</headline>
<dateline>WEST COVINA, Calif. 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SOUTHWEST WATER COMPANY FINANCIAL HIGHLIGHTS</p>
<p>			   Three Months Ended	Year Ended</p>
<p>			     December 31,	     December 31,</p>
<p>			1996(a)     1995(a)     1996(a)  1995(a)(b)</p>
<p>				   (unaudited)	  (audited)</p>
<p>Operating</p>
<p>  revenues    $16,242,000 $15,340,000 $66,145,000 $56,807,000</p>
<p> Net income	 619,000     556,000   1,923,000   1,439,000</p>
<p>Earnings per</p>
<p>  common share	  .20	   .18	   .61	   .46</p>
<p>Weighted average outstanding shares</p>
<p>used in earnings per common share</p>
<p>  computation   3,122,000   3,091,000   3,112,000   3,076,000</p>
<p>NOTE: (a)  Per share amounts and outstanding shares reflect a 20 percent stock dividend on January 2, 1997 and a five percent stock dividend on January 2, 1996.</p>
<p>(b)  Results for 1995 include a net gain of $105,000 due to recovery of disputed property tax assessments in the second quarter of 1995, and a net gain of $50,000, or $.02 per common share, from the sale of land in the first quarter of 1995.</p>
